# SRG-APP-000141-AU-000090  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must be configured to disable non-essential
# capabilities.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000141-AU-000090
group:           V-221920
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000381
control_rev5:    CM-7

contribution:    Splunk can turn each role-bearing service on an instance on or off
                 independently - Splunk Web, the KV Store, and distributed search - so that
                 an instance carries only the roles its deployment design calls for.

governs:         distsearch.conf - How a search head reaches the indexers it searches.
governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           server.conf [kvstore] disabled present
check:           distsearch.conf [distributedSearch] disabled present
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] startwebserver https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] startwebserver present
                 reason: "startwebserver = [0 | 1]. Set whether or not to start Splunk Web.
                         0 disables Splunk Web, 1 enables it. Default: 1"
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Which roles a given instance is meant to carry, which comes from the
                 distributed deployment design and the system security plan; the product
                 STIG check reads the Monitoring Console mode and the role assignment, and
                 marks a standalone installation not applicable because every function it
                 provides is then necessary.
external:        Non-essential capabilities of the host outside the application - operating
                 system services, packages, and browser plug-ins on analyst workstations -
                 carried by the operating system and the workstation build.

citation:        SPLK-CL-000300 check and fix text; web.conf.spec:23 (startwebserver = [0 |
                 1], default 1), server.conf.spec:5234 (kvstore disabled, default false),
                 distsearch.conf.spec:36 (distributedSearch disabled, default false)
finding:         The role-bearing services the application can switch off - Splunk Web, the
                 KV Store, and distributed search - are left at their shipped defaults
                 rather than declared for this instance's role, so the configuration does
                 not show that only the necessary capabilities are enabled.
